4871:## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals
4874:- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.
4875:- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for "a new version only Alex opens" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.
4876:- **Where written:** AGENTS.md, "Authority and scope" (the D439 bullet) and §7.3 "Own the loop"; `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`; the memory file `feedback-council-decides-while-alex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.
4879:## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)

codex
**I would not adopt A1 as written.** Clamping can be a useful compatibility option, but only if every caller can see the date actually served. Until that contract is designed and checked, refusal is the clearer behavior for an explicit date that includes unfinished work.

The reason is visible in the existing interfaces: `/views`, `/evidence`, and `/changes` return arrays, including empty arrays, with no place for `served_as_of`. Several MCP tools return those arrays directly. Adding a label therefore requires a deliberate response-contract change or another reliably exposed channel; it cannot be accomplished solely inside `resolve_bound`. A range request whose `since` or `from` is after the clamped end also needs an explicit outcome: an unlabelled empty result could be mistaken for “nothing changed.” [API routes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_api.py:164), [MCP tools](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_mcp.py:77), [changes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:269).

There is also a gap in A1’s state rule. A store that has no unfinished work *now* may acquire an unfinished day immediately after the request’s snapshot. Allowing future bounds on that basis changes the earlier contract’s rule for a live store, and clients may receive different treatment for the same date depending on when they ask. Specify finished and live stores independently of whether partial rows happen to be present, and test the transition. [Current contract](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:50).

D439 permits the council to decide a reversible service change while Alex is inactive, provided the decision is reviewed, recorded and measured within its limits. It does **not** itself authorize deploying or publishing the changed running service. I would bring the product-facing response and compatibility design back to the council before implementation, and record the eventual choice for Alex. [D439](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4871).

The census is a material reason to do that design: the proposed resolver affects historical and production stores as well as new-system live stores. I verified the default store path in the API and the relevant code paths; I did **not** independently reproduce the database census or the 99/117 counts. [API default](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/hivemind_api.py:205).

CONSENSUS: no, because clamp-with-label is not yet defined for every response shape or range, and the live-to-finished transition needs a consistent rule.
